{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/675860-the-hardest-game-to-run-and-why","id":675860,"title":"The hardest game to Run and why?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-09-23T18:04:05-07:00","id":675860,"title":"The hardest game to Run and why?","content":"been playing for 10 years now. faced many challenges as a GM. but the question is - in your own opinion - which are the hardest game's to GM/DM and Why?<br /> <br /> i dont know WHY but i still have troubles soaking in Changeling..probably because im a dark guy and more into sorrow and hatred than Hope...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forum's Official's Joker and Trickster. Pardon my bad english, aint my first language (I Speak Spanish).<br /> ST: DtF, HtR, WtO, MtA<br /> Signature Chars: Crowley (hakalu), Joe The Nuwisha (WtA)<br /> Changelings: be afraid of the Technocracian High Five of Doom","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley","name":"Crowley","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1754_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-23T18:34:12-07:00","id":675894,"title":"","content":"I'd have to say Wraith: the Oblivion because of its baggage and the misconceptions of the game, its hard to get anyone to play it. And Shadowguiding could be a mess if the players aren't up for the task.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://youtu.be/_yBS2EZFduI?t=2m13s\" target=\"_blank\">Homo sapiens. What an inventive, invincible species. It's only a few million years since they crawled up out of the mud and learned to walk. Puny, defenceless bipeds. They've survived flood, famine and plague. They've survived cosmic wars and holocausts. And now, here they are, out among the stars, waiting to begin a new life. Ready to outsit eternity. They're indomitable. Indomitable.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/420-akatsukileader13","name":"AkatsukiLeader13","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar420_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1637"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-23T19:38:04-07:00","id":675961,"title":"","content":"For my money, it's Wraith. Very difficult game to play. At least, for me it is. However, I have a good feeling that Rich Dansky is going to do a hell of a lot to change that for Wraith 20.<br /> <br /> With that said, I love, love, LOVE the lore and setting of Wraith so damn much. But damn is it a difficult game to run for a number of reasons.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">&quot;Steel isn't strong, boy. Flesh is stronger.&quot;</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/95-fat-larry","name":"Fat Larry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar95_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-24T01:16:49-07:00","id":676158,"title":"","content":"I have to say Wraith. It's a testament to its mood and tone, but it's hard to get everyone on the same page for Wraith, and as much as I like the thing, there are times when the whole affair actually brings me down. And as much as I am impressed by it, I have a hard time running, as do quite a few people playing something that's made to elicit such a dark and somber mood.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-24T12:14:33-07:00","id":676707,"title":"","content":"I've only run Mage, Demon and Vampire, personally, but of those three, Vampire was the hardest for me. I've never really had a good grasp of the tone or feeling of the game, and my players followed my lead, or lack thereof. Let's just say, we went Vampion very quickly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2430-kalinara","name":"kalinara","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2430_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"582"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-25T13:11:36-07:00","id":677913,"title":"","content":"Dark Ages: Fae. I love this game, my favorite by far. As a storyteller, coming up with plots is hard as hell though! It desperately needed a storyteller companion","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3075-coridan","name":"Coridan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3075_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"528"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-27T08:08:24-07:00","id":680040,"title":"","content":"Where the world of darkness is concerned, I'm not sure that I'd actually say that I consider any of the game lines hard to run... I mean, I've had troubles with more than a few of them, but that always came down to me not really &quot;getting it&quot; (changeling just doesn't get absorbed no matter how much I read it, for example) or my group of players not really being into what the story was about (one player actually managed to articulate the issue by saying &quot;I just don't know what I'm supposed to do or care about in-character - the game doesn't really present goals and behaviors that are 'the standard fare' like how Dungeons &amp; Dragons presents that characters are adventures and what a typical adventure is like&quot; so I could start working on the issue, having him play in a few campaigns which had a more direct and immediate story-line and more input from me what the characters should be like and care about).<br /> <br /> But when I compare any of the World of Darkness games to, well, let's use Shadowrun 3rd edition as an example... they are easy as breathing to run.<br /> <br /> That said, I've really only successfully run Vampire, various mortal-only campaigns, and Hunter: the Reckoning with any amount of success. The other games each ran into some obstacle that was found to be insurmountable at the time... changeling I just couldn't get into my head, demon burned out because my players and I had incompatible views of the game's intended style, wraith became a bad word because of players being jerks to each other on purpose and trying to use the game as an excuse/permission, mage didn't work because my players at the time wouldn't stop arguing about whatever difficulty I figured their spell to be (along the lines of &quot;What do you mean it is vulgar magic to make electricity arc 15 feet from that light fixture to the guy standing next to the car?! The car is wet metal!&quot;), Werewolf seemed cool but I have yet to find a group of players that find the same things cool as I do so all the chronicles I tried to participate in felt like two completely different games going on (the one I was playing, and the one everyone else was).<br /> <br /> And I can't really put a reason to why I haven't played the other classic games... I guess no one really brought them up around me or something.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Not so noble anymore.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1823-drake","name":"Drake","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1823_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"456"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-27T09:09:49-07:00","id":680073,"title":"","content":"Wraith is notoriously difficult to run and plan in simply because of the burden it places not just on the storyteller but the players as well. A game can blow up in any number of ways but few games are as likely to blow up in everyone's face like a Wraith game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3065-nist498","name":"Nist498","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3065_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"72"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-29T18:41:17-07:00","id":682570,"title":"","content":"Changeling I've found a doddle. Even my current Changeling/Mage game has been interesting (I pitched it as a kind of World of Darkness Neverwhere, set in the shared magical places of Manchester), and while we've had a lot of changes of players (something I see a lot of in play by post games, to be honest), we've really settled in and got a good balance of characters now (50/50 between the two character types, with each requiring the other to some degree). So any issues I had before balancing the two games' themes have gradually disappeared.<br /> <br /> Wraith I've struggled with just because no one managed to put together a character for the game I ran, and the game I played in lost its ST to RL stuff. People struggled once it came to Passions and Fetters. But I had more ideas for this game than for any other.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-01T19:57:11-07:00","id":685159,"title":"","content":"Changeling and I will sum it up with one question: What happens when you climb a chimerical ladder?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-03T15:55:41-07:00","id":687602,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/675860-the-hardest-game-to-run-and-why?p=685159#post685159\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Changeling and I will sum it up with one question: What happens when you climb a chimerical ladder?</div> </div> </div> </div>You rise through the air. In all-fae company, they'll see you climbing the ladder. If humans are there, you'll appear to be ascending of your own accord. Their disbelief may mean you get shunted into the Dreaming, however, unless you overcome their Banality.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-03T15:59:33-07:00","id":687610,"title":"","content":"In some interpretations of the RAW, chimerical reality could be entirely delusional. But that interpretation would be wrong. Even though only the fae can usually see it, chimerical reality does have an objective existence beyond the lunacy of faeries.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-07T21:12:19-07:00","id":693449,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>adambeyoncelowe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/675860-the-hardest-game-to-run-and-why?p=687602#post687602\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You rise through the air. In all-fae company, they'll see you climbing the ladder. If humans are there, you'll appear to be ascending of your own accord. Their disbelief may mean you get shunted into the Dreaming, however, unless you overcome their Banality.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> As Adam said above... But I'll add; interestingly a similar problem occurs when say a Troll tries to squeeze himself into a small car. He can do it, but he has to deny his Seeming. Basically, he shuts down his Fae self and can manage it in his mortal form. But this rejection of his Faerie nature results in Banality.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7861-strafe","name":"Strafe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"18"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-07T21:21:15-07:00","id":693458,"title":"","content":"Wraith by a mile.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-08T05:47:56-07:00","id":693788,"title":"","content":"Demon the Fallen for me. As someone who grew up fairly secularly, how the hell does one accurately portray Faith and the reaping of it? What makes someone look at the demon and go &quot;I put my faith in you&quot; instead of going &quot;holy shit, ruuuunnnnn&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://madnessforums.com/forums/index.php\" target=\"_blank\">Malkavian Madness Forum</a> - Your pbp fix. Be it nWoD, cWoD, CoC, D&amp;D or something else entirely, come over here and get your game on","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/348-infernalgoose","name":"InfernalGoose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"390"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-03T05:15:56-08:00","id":751184,"title":"","content":"(Glanced at other responses, but just jumping in and not addressing anyone in particular...)<br /> <br /> Like the consensus seems to say, &quot;Wraith&quot; is a tricky one for many players/STs because, as presented, it *really* takes a lot of mental investment in terms of characterization than any other splat. (You can always make up &quot;yet another Toreador&quot;, what-have-you, as an on-the-spot character to play, but it's really trickier with Wraith, as you really have to &quot;go deep&quot; to come up with a properly justifiable character who would continue to exist after death.)<br /> <br /> Changeling is sort of on the flip of that, and while not *quite* as hard meta-conceptually, it can be tricky for some players because you ultimately have to understand the dynamics involved. That is, instead of having to &quot;go deep&quot; for reasons to exist a la' Wraith, you have to understand how to be essentially the dynamic &quot;oomph&quot; that makes life/existence worth living (even with the more mopey types, such as the Sluagh, there is the undeniable sense of continuation and &quot;fae-ness&quot; that resonates). It's sort of like understanding what makes a really good stand-up comedian *funny* -- anyone can be &quot;funny&quot;, or be quite humorous, but it's *work* and a measure of talent and experience to make a *comedian* (read: Changeling) happen. (That doesn't mean said character has to be &quot;funny&quot;, rather I am just drawing a distinction between someone being &quot;funny&quot; -- a typical character from most of the other splats -- and being a &quot;comedian&quot; -- representing the unique flavor and essence that being a Changeling or Fae represents... it's a hard thing for some people to process...).<br /> <br /> Still, though, for either Wraith or Changeling, the key is getting into character and roleplay, roleplay, roleplay. While this &quot;should be&quot; the case for virtually all characters created, it's very much more so the key for these to splats above any of the others. I've noted over the almost 25 years of WoD (and the proto-versions of Changelings and Wraiths play-tested at the early MET Larps before the hardcovers, proper, came out) that it's more so (not always, but usually) the pwrgmrz and the &quot;I essentially always play myself&quot; players who have the most trouble with those two games/splats. Anyone, of course, might have trouble for various reasons -- not &quot;getting&quot; the setting, or understanding that you can tweak/alter various aspects to better fit your own tastes/views -- but generally the key is to roleplay the fuck out of the characters in question and &quot;step-it-up&quot; if you're not accustomed to doing so. That's usually been the &quot;Eureka!&quot;-moment for a number of players I've seen have problems with them over the years but who suddenly &quot;got it&quot; -- they went deep and found the solution was there the entire time....","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have been around here for waaaayyyy too fucking long...","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1433-just-john-forever","name":"Just John, Forever...","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-03T06:54:12-08:00","id":751328,"title":"","content":"Creating characters in Wraith, especially, can be hard. I usually let new players create their Shadows after the first session (they can be played like the P'o in KotE if they need to appear in the first session) and give a bit of leeway in tweaking starting stats once they figure out what works in play. A helpful ST can also sketch out a character concept with a player, then draw up suggested traits, and let the player tweak them as needed. That's worked for me to help players overcome their initial fears about the complexity of character creation. I enjoy creating characters anyway, so it's not too much of a problem.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-03T08:14:37-08:00","id":751476,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>InfernalGoose</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/675860-the-hardest-game-to-run-and-why?p=693788#post693788\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Demon the Fallen for me. As someone who grew up fairly secularly, how the hell does one accurately portray Faith and the reaping of it? What makes someone look at the demon and go &quot;I put my faith in you&quot; instead of going &quot;holy shit, ruuuunnnnn&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>its somewhat connected to that.<br /> <br /> the way i see it, the reaping of faith comes from the idea of making humanity accept that they are wrong. to break their paradigma.<br /> <br /> By admiting the existance of something beyond their control and comprehention, inadvertily makes them be aware of the existance of something else (be god or some other entity).<br /> <br /> basically, we can sum it up as &quot;I exist, you see me. now you understand how little are your ideas...now, do you believe in me? run.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forum's Official's Joker and Trickster. Pardon my bad english, aint my first language (I Speak Spanish).<br /> ST: DtF, HtR, WtO, MtA<br /> Signature Chars: Crowley (hakalu), Joe The Nuwisha (WtA)<br /> Changelings: be afraid of the Technocracian High Five of Doom","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley","name":"Crowley","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1754_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-03T11:01:24-08:00","id":751725,"title":"","content":"I've only recently started reading into classic and planning to run a game there, so my experience with this is nonexistent and solely based on guesswork. That said, I think Wraith would be the hardest. Primarily because all the other games take place in the real world, while Wraith takes place, mostly, in the Underworld. It's one thing for you to run a world that is basically 'our world, but darker,' where there's a sinister agenda behind not-McDonalds, school systems are manipulated by the conspiracies and so forth. It's another for the Underworld, which is not our world, but is a darker reflection of it. It seems like there's a lot more work to be done building the setting and getting players to understand the differences and what the Underworld is like.<br /> <br /> I'm sure this isn't a problem everyone has, but I've also struggled to get my players to embrace the concept of the Dark Ages. They are worried they will not appreciate the differences enough and aren't interested enough in history to really know what's available and what's going on, so they may make a faux pas and try to use concepts that didn't exist yet.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-22T12:32:16-08:00","id":771649,"title":"","content":"I never played or STd Wraith, so can't argue it. Demon isn't such a problem. The best definition I could give of Faith is confidence. It isn't about running from a monster because it is huge, scary, and unknowable. It is because you somehow, without need for further proof, <u>know</u> it is Incarnate Evil TM. Of course anyone who sees a Devourer in Apocalyptic Form is likely to run away because it is a freaking scary monster. But to have Faith is to &quot;know&quot; it is a &quot;demon from hell&quot;, not just use such words because you can't think better ones.<br /> <br /> My greatest problem in cWoD is with Mage. To be precise, with the Seek. I do have a good grasp of the concept, but failed to actually run a good one.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-26T21:52:33-07:00","id":875265,"title":"","content":"So far i have done Vampire, vampire DA, werewolf, Werewolf DA, and the oriental Kuen-ji .. For me i would say the latter is the harder to run more cause it seems a lot harder for them to not fall down and go splat with the whole Dharma stuff (and even after reading the book like half a dozen times i still don't understand everything).. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11674-garhkal","name":"garhkal","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11674_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"547"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-05T02:28:41-07:00","id":882698,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>InfernalGoose</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/675860-the-hardest-game-to-run-and-why?p=693788#post693788\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Demon the Fallen for me. As someone who grew up fairly secularly, how the hell does one accurately portray Faith and the reaping of it? What makes someone look at the demon and go &quot;I put my faith in you&quot; instead of going &quot;holy shit, ruuuunnnnn&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>The Demon smiles, holds out his scaly red hand and says &quot;Don't <b>be</b> afraid. Just put your <b>trust</b> in me and <i><b>nothing bad</b> will happen <b>to you</b></i>.&quot; Granted, many humans would run at this point - this is why it's important to corner the human before doing such a thing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3254,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","user":"Muad'Dib","date":". 05-05-2016, 05:33 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}